# Database & Model Conventions

MongoDB models, Mongoose schemas, and database operation patterns.

## Model Structure

```typescript
// Standard NestJS Mongoose model
import { Prop, Schema, SchemaFactory } from '@nestjs/mongoose'
import { Document, Schema as MongooseSchema } from 'mongoose'
import { FormStatusEnum } from '@heyform-inc/shared-types-enums'
import { nanoid } from '@heyform-inc/utils'

@Schema({
  timestamps: true,     // Auto-add createdAt, updatedAt
  toJSON: { virtuals: true }
})
export class FormModel extends Document {
  @Prop({ default: () => nanoid(8) })
  _id: string         // Custom IDs (not ObjectId)

  @Prop({ required: true, index: true })
  teamId: string

  @Prop({
    type: Number,
    required: true,
    enum: Object.values(FormStatusEnum).filter(v => typeof v === 'number'),
    default: FormStatusEnum.NORMAL
  })
  status: FormStatusEnum

  @Prop({ type: MongooseSchema.Types.Mixed })
  settings?: FormSettings

  @Prop({ default: [], type: [MongooseSchema.Types.Mixed] })
  fields?: FormField[]
}

export const FormSchema = SchemaFactory.createForClass(FormModel)

// Compound indexes after schema creation
FormSchema.index({ teamId: 1, projectId: 1 }, { unique: false })
```

**Conventions**:
- Extend `Document` from mongoose
- Use `@Schema({ timestamps: true })` for auto timestamps
- Export both class and schema
- File naming: `{domain}.model.ts`
- Custom IDs: `nanoid(8)` (strings, not ObjectIds)
- Index frequently queried fields: `index: true`

## Property Patterns

```typescript
// Required fields
@Prop({ required: true, index: true })
teamId: string

// Optional with default
@Prop({ default: false })
isActive?: boolean

// Enums (filter by type!)
@Prop({
  type: Number,
  enum: Object.values(FormStatusEnum).filter(v => typeof v === 'number'),
  default: FormStatusEnum.NORMAL
})
status: FormStatusEnum

// Complex objects
@Prop({ type: MongooseSchema.Types.Mixed })
settings?: FormSettings

// Arrays
@Prop({ default: [], type: [MongooseSchema.Types.Mixed] })
fields?: FormField[]

// Maps/Records
@Prop({ type: Map, default: {} })
config?: Record<string, any>

// Unix timestamps
@Prop({ default: 0 })
publishedAt?: number

// Unique fields
@Prop({ default: () => nanoid(), unique: true })
inviteCode: string
```

## Indexes

```typescript
// Single field index
@Prop({ required: true, index: true })
formId: string

// Compound indexes (after schema creation)
FormSchema.index({ teamId: 1, projectId: 1 }, { unique: false })
TeamMemberSchema.index({ teamId: 1, memberId: 1 }, { unique: true })
IntegrationSchema.index({ formId: 1, appId: 1 }, { unique: true })
```

**Index Rules**:
- Index fields used in queries
- Compound indexes for multi-field queries
- Mark unique indexes explicitly

## Virtual Properties

```typescript
// Computed properties (not stored)
FormSchema.virtual('isDraft').get(function () {
  return helper.isEmpty(this.fields) && this.version === 0
})

// Parse JSON virtuals
FormSchema.virtual('drafts').get(function () {
  if (helper.isValid(this._drafts)) {
    const drafts = parseJson(this._drafts)
    if (helper.isValidArray(drafts)) return drafts
  }
  return this.fields || []
})
```

**Rules**:
- Use `function()` syntax (not arrow) to access `this`
- Virtuals not stored in DB
- Enable with `toJSON: { virtuals: true }`

